virglrenderer: flush after resource and transfer commands from QEMU

What: after creating or freeing a resource, after a transfer to the host and
after destroying a context (QEMU's resource create/unref, transfer-to-host and
context destroy commands), glFlush() on the context the work ran on, mostly
vrend's own context ctx0. A transfer with a guest context id is not flushed:
guest contexts are flushed by their fences, and Mesa sends many per frame.
Why: nothing else flushes ctx0 (guest contexts are flushed by their fences),
and Apple's GL keeps the memory of textures made, deleted or uploaded on a
context until that context is flushed. Every guest mode change uploads the new
screen through QEMU's 2D path on ctx0, so a guest switching modes in a loop
grew QEMU's "IOAccelerator (graphics)" memory without end even after
qemu-cocoa-gl-view-flush.patch (3840x2160 <-> 2560x1440: about 16 MB per
switch; flat with this patch). Found by flushing ctx0 after every QEMU command
in a test build.
Upstream: not sent (macOS driver behaviour).
Tests: tests/graphics/scanout-churn.sh (test VM; IOAccelerator memory over
120 mode switches).
--- a/src/virglrenderer.c
